      "value": "Did some further testing:\n\nIn Looping:Reverse mode, the dolly moves from node 1 to node 2, then pauses for the added length of all other paths. So in my example above, it travels from node 1 to node 2 in 15 seconds, then pauses until the 45 second mark before moving on.\n\nIn Looping:Repeat mode, it does the same as Reverse, except it ONLY goes from node 1 to node 2, then snaps back to node 1 at the 45 second mark, completely ignoring the other nodes on the paths.\n\nChanging Path Type to Fitted or Linear has no effect on the timing issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
