  "details": "I use the dolly cam in multicam/Spout mode for streaming and it used to function as expected, but for several months now the timing has been completely wrong.\n\nI'll set up three camera paths\n\nI set the Duration to 15 seconds and don't change it\n\nFor each path I only set up four nodes, totaling 60 seconds per path\n\nTHE PROBLEM: Instead of each path cycling for 60 seconds and repeating, they cycle once (60 seconds) then pause at their starting points for another 2 minutes before cycling again.\n\nI'm guessing that the timing is adding ALL the path times together instead of using the longest one (pausing the shorter paths, if any, until the longest one has reached its end).\n\nIn case it matters, my camera settings are:\n\nPaths: 3\n\nMotion Control: Time (required for multicam)\n\nEasing: None\n\nPath Type: Loose\n\nLooping: Revolve\n\nCapture: None\n\nStreaming: Multi",
